## Scenario 3: Multi-Agent Research System

**3.1 (Domain 1)** — Coordinator's system prompt says delegate, but it never spawns subagents; attempts all research itself. Cause?
A. Model tier too small
B. Subagents must be started manually
C. Prompt needs "delegate" capitalized
D. Coordinator's `allowedTools` doesn't include "Task" — the mechanism for spawning subagents

**3.2 (Domain 1)** — Web search subagent gathers great findings; synthesis subagent's reports are generic, referencing nothing. Coordinator just says "Synthesize the research findings." What's wrong?
A. Synthesis agent needs extended thinking
B. Subagents don't inherit coordinator's conversation history — coordinator must include actual findings directly in the synthesis prompt
C. Synthesis agent needs its own web search tools
D. Prompt needs "please"

**3.3 (Domain 1)** — Coordinator invokes search subagent, waits, then invokes analysis subagent — doubling latency despite independence. How to parallelize?
A. Emit both Task tool calls in a single response, spawning subagents in parallel
B. Ask each subagent to work faster
C. Run two copies of the whole system
D. Parallelism is impossible for subagents

**3.4 (Domain 1)** — Coordinator gives subagents rigid step-by-step scripts; they fail on topics that don't fit. Better design?
A. Make procedures longer
B. Remove all instructions
C. Specify research goals and quality criteria; let subagent adapt its approach
D. Have subagents ask a human whenever the script fails

**3.5 (Domain 1)** — Reports are coherent but shallow on some subtopics. Want self-detection/repair of coverage gaps. Which pattern?
A. Accept first synthesis as final
B. Iterative refinement loop: coordinator evaluates synthesis for gaps, re-delegates targeted queries, re-invokes synthesis until sufficient
C. Ask report generator to pad thin sections with general knowledge
D. Always run every subagent exactly twice

**3.6 (Domain 2)** — All subagents get the full 18-tool catalog; synthesis tries web search, search tries document parsing. Correct redesign?
A. Add a 19th tool that tells agents which tool to use
B. Alphabetize the tool list
C. Write longer prompts warning agents off certain tools
D. Scope each subagent's tool set to its role — a handful of relevant tools each

**3.7 (Domain 2)** — Subagents burn many calls just discovering what data exists before real work begins. Which MCP capability reduces this?
A. Expose content catalogs (document hierarchies, schemas) as MCP resources, giving visibility without exploratory tool calls
B. Increase tool-call budget
C. Hard-code current inventory into every system prompt
D. Remove discovery capability

**3.8 (Domain 5)** — Final reports cite nothing; each summarization step strips source attribution. Structural fix?
A. Report generator adds plausible citations at the end
B. Instruct synthesis to write "sources available on request"
C. Require subagents to output structured claim-source mappings (claim, evidence, source) that every downstream agent preserves through synthesis
D. Reduce summarization steps to one

**3.9 (Domain 5, select TWO)** — Two credible sources report different market-size figures; one subagent picked the larger number. Which TWO practices are correct?
A. Annotate the conflict explicitly (both values + attribution); let coordinator decide reconciliation **✓**
B. Average the two figures
C. Always adopt the more recent source, discard the other
D. Require publication/data-collection dates in structured outputs, so temporal differences aren't misread as contradictions **✓**
E. Exclude both sources

**3.10 (Domain 5, select TWO)** — How should the web search subagent behave when searches fail or return nothing? Which TWO behaviors are correct?
A. On any failure, terminate the entire workflow
B. Attempt local recovery for transient failures; propagate only unresolved errors, including what was attempted and partial results **✓**
C. Return empty results marked as success on failure
D. Report every problem as generic "search unavailable"
E. Distinguish access failures (timeouts/errors) from valid empty results (successful queries, no matches) **✓**

